  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The paper develops an end-to-end, IIIF-based pipeline that extracts, parses, and geocodes commercial advertisements from the 20th-century digitised Armenian press of France. To overcome the lack of off-the-shelf OCR models for Western Armenian, the pipeline uses vision-language models (VLMs) to process curved scans and generate structured records. The authors release a 500-page Western Armenian press corpus containing 3,270 advertisement-level annotations, alongside a unified Label Studio annotation template.",
      "why": "It establishes a reproducible workflow that allows researchers to extract structured spatial data from historical corpora in under-resourced languages without relying on pre-existing, high-quality OCR models."
    }
